-- Enrich the V2/V5/V6 sample activities with coherent GPS streams.
--
-- Why: V5 attached route polylines to the wrong activities (ids 4-14 are
-- shifted by 3 — e.g. the "Golden Gate Run" track ended up on "Interval
-- Training"), no seeded activity had point_timestamps (so split tables fell
-- back to a uniform average-pace estimate everywhere), and none had heart
-- rate. This migration regenerates, per outdoor activity:
--   * route_polyline     - Google-encoded track anchored in the activity's
--                          real city, haversine length == stored distance
--   * point_timestamps   - epoch seconds per point (start_time + offset),
--                          with workout-appropriate pace variation so splits
--                          are individually meaningful
--   * elevation_profile  - per-point altitude, positive deltas == elevation_gain
--   * average/max heart rate, and average power for rides
-- Indoor pool swims (3, 10, 20) keep their single-point polyline and only
-- receive heart-rate values.
--
-- Generated deterministically; regenerate with the script kept in the PR
-- description if the sample data ever changes.

